Agern for Debian and Ubuntu
===========================

Files
  /usr/bin/agern                   the control command (agern help)
  /usr/share/agern/agern.jar       the server, with the web frontend embedded
  /etc/agern/agern.env             configuration (root:agern 0640), created on first install with
                                   a fresh FACTORY_MASTER_KEY and never overwritten by upgrades
  /var/lib/agern                   data: git workspaces, per-user homes (home of the 'agern' user)
  /var/cache/agern                 current.deb / previous.deb kept for 'agern rollback' (root)
  agern.service                    the server, runs as the unprivileged 'agern' user
  agern-upgrade.timer/.service     automatic upgrades, off by default ('agern auto-upgrade on')
  agern-sandbox.socket/.service    rootless Podman for build/test sandboxes, as the 'agern' user;
                                   off by default ('agern sandbox enable', which names the packages
                                   to install); storage in /var/lib/agern/containers
  agern-sandbox-prune.timer        daily removal of unused sandbox images (on with sandboxes)
  logs                             journald: 'agern logs' or 'journalctl -u agern'

First steps
  sudo apt install postgresql && sudo agern setup-db
  sudo apt install chromium fonts-noto-core   # recommended: the UI reviewers' headless browser
  sudoedit /etc/agern/agern.env    # FACTORY_GITHUB_ORG, FACTORY_PUBLIC_URL, FACTORY_ADMINS, FACTORY_AUTH
  sudo agern doctor && sudo agern start

Removing
  apt remove agern   keeps configuration, data, the 'agern' user and the database
  apt purge agern    also removes /etc/agern/agern.env (a copy goes to /var/backups), the
                     package cache, the sandbox storage /var/lib/agern/containers and the
                     'agern' user; the rest of /var/lib/agern and the database stay

Full guide: https://github.com/Egernet-CS/agern/blob/main/docs/INSTALL-LINUX.md
